  <rules>
    <rule name="Daemonic Animosity" id="93e2-4115-0c37-8605" hidden="true" page="51" publicationId="02e1-3f69-7ae7-f5c5">
      <description>Whenever you have daemons of rival Chaos Gods within 12&quot; of each other at the start of your turn, and they are not engaged in close combat, make a Daemon Animosity test for each Greater Daemon or each unit of Daemons to determine how it reacts to the proximity of its closest rivals. This does not affect daemonic creatures used as mounts or rewards
1-2: Remove the rivals from play, but don&apos;t count as destroyed for VP
3-4: The daemons will not move or do anything else this turn, but can fight back if in close combat
5-6: Continue normally with no further effect</description>
    </rule>
  </rules>
