  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Aura of Slaanesh" id="58d9-2859-54a2-0a61" hidden="false" page="55" publicationId="02e1-3f69-7ae7-f5c5">
      <description>In close ocmbat enemy models must test against their Leadership on 3D6 to be able to strike this model. If they fail the test then they fight normally, but if they win the combat they will not strike the model so any hits are wasted and the combat as treated as a draw. If the enemy model passes the test they do not need to test it again.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Beast of Nurgle Attacks" id="11e9-a5b4-f0c3-5cc7" hidden="false" page="58" publicationId="02e1-3f69-7ae7-f5c5">
      <description>The Beast of Nurgle has D6 Attacks in close combat, check each round. No armour saving throw is permitted for models wounded by the Beast</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Blood Scent" id="addd-de39-dcab-a95d" hidden="false" page="54" publicationId="02e1-3f69-7ae7-f5c5">
      <description>Flesh Hounds do not have to charge the nearest enemy model when they charge. Instead they may charge any enemy model that is within range.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Bound" id="fe02-db2c-cd6c-35be" hidden="false" page="60" publicationId="02e1-3f69-7ae7-f5c5">
      <description>Flamers can move over any obstacles or intervening models without penalty</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Cloud of Flies" id="8671-aac0-7a74-9080" hidden="false" page="58" publicationId="02e1-3f69-7ae7-f5c5">
      <description>Any enemy fighting a Plaguebearer must deduct -1 from their close combat score</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Crush" id="9110-c3b3-b696-8583" hidden="false" page="54" publicationId="02e1-3f69-7ae7-f5c5">
      <description>If the Juggernaut charges into close combat then its attacks count as Crush attacks for that turn. If the Juggernaut wins the combat round then it automatically causes 1 wound for each hit struck regardless of the enemy&apos;s Toughness and ignoring any armour
The Crush can also be used on vehicles. When fighting all attacks hit automatically and the attacker can choose the location struck. In the case of the Juggernaut the standard penetration is a 5 + 2D6. When making a Crush attack the Juggernaut&apos;s penetration is increased by a further D6 to 5 + 3D6</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Disc Movement" id="1de1-b9e9-5818-2574" hidden="false" page="60" publicationId="02e1-3f69-7ae7-f5c5">
      <description>The Disc moves at head height. This as treated as normal movement penalties apply except that a Disc may move over water, marshes or other soft ground without penalty</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Furious Charge" id="0cd4-2e22-e9b4-e7ed" hidden="false" page="31" publicationId="02e1-3f69-7ae7-f5c5">
      <description>Units with this rule triple their movement when they charge instead of doubling it. However, each model can only use this bonus if it allows it to get into close combat that turn. The tripled charge move may not be used by models that are not able to reach the enemy. This bonus also applies to any character model that has joined the unit, and who is on foot</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Flame Attacks" id="1c1b-11fc-17f6-8ae5" hidden="false" page="60" publicationId="02e1-3f69-7ae7-f5c5">
      <description>Flamers can shoot flame in the shooting phase. The flame has a 6&quot; range and any target struck sustains D6 S3 hits.
In close combat a successful strike from a Flamer causes D3 wounds</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Fly" id="1eae-bc57-fb7b-9461" hidden="false" page="52" publicationId="02e1-3f69-7ae7-f5c5">
      <description>The model can fly using the same rules as a Jump Pack

Can move 18&quot; in a straight line, or 12&quot; if jumping a single story building. Remove a further 6&quot; for each story higher.
+4&quot; to charge move after landing

Further rules in Wargear book Pg. 71</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Infestations" id="698e-25d4-994f-5cfc" hidden="false" page="57" publicationId="02e1-3f69-7ae7-f5c5">
      <description>Any Nurglings included in an army may be set up at the start of the battle if you want, and do not have to be summoned to the battlefield. Note that you can choose to summon Nurglings if you wish, it&apos;s just that you don&apos;t have to. 
Nurglings cannot be banished back to the warp.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Juggernaut Calavry" id="691d-d72e-e26c-645b" hidden="false" page="54" publicationId="02e1-3f69-7ae7-f5c5">
      <description>When shooting at the Juggernaut and its rider roll to hit as normal, but randomize any hits between rider and mount. Work out any hits as normal and resolve damage against either the rider or the Juggernaut. If the rider is slain the Juggernaut may continue to fight on its own. If the Juggernaut is slain the rider can continue to fight on its own. 
In the case of attacks from weapons with a burst area, treat the rider and Juggernaut as separate targets, so both will be hit if both lie within the template.
In close combat both the Juggernaut and its rider fight separately. In effect, this works the same way as a multiple combat. Any enemy may choose to aim its attack at either the rider of the Juggernaut</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Nurgle War Altar Damage Table" id="2210-d381-f879-f3b6" hidden="false">
      <description>1: Track*
2-3: Hull
4: Sponson*
5: Turret
6: Throne of Nurgle
*Hit the one nearest to Attacker
See datafax for damage table 1-5

6: If the shot hits the Throne of Nurgle then the blast has hit the throne&apos;s Conversion Field. If the shot gets through this energy field then it will strike the High Priest Rancidguts. Roll to wound him as normal. If the High Priest is killed the Throne of Nurgle will no longer provide protection from psychic powers from the psychic field.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Plague Knife" id="17c3-8ed1-aa82-dd8c" hidden="false">
      <description>A wound from this weapon will kill mortal creatures on a D6 roll of a 6 regardless of how many wounds the target can sustain normally. On a 1-5, it inflicts 1 wound.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Regeneration" id="9065-0dfd-542f-78c1" hidden="false" page="53" publicationId="02e1-3f69-7ae7-f5c5">
      <description>Place slain Bloodletters on their side instead of removing them from play. In the rally phase at the end of the turn roll a D6 for each Bloodletter model. On a 4+ it regenerates any damage it suffered and stands back up, otherwise it is removed from play.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Riding Beast" id="9ea5-7129-5842-6417" hidden="false" page="56" publicationId="02e1-3f69-7ae7-f5c5">
      <description>Follows all the rules for Cavalry in the rulebook. Note that the effect of a mounts daemonic aura does not apply if the daemon is ridden by a mortal Champion. When ridden by a mortal Champion the normal armour saving throw of the Champion applies instead.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Slime Trail" id="6867-1cd7-a670-ba83" hidden="false" page="58" publicationId="02e1-3f69-7ae7-f5c5">
      <description>Multiple attackers do not receive the usual bonuses when attacking the Beast, no +1 for extra Attack for each opponent after the first, nor the +1 close combat modifier for each opponent after the first.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Soporific Musk" id="d53d-9264-e3ab-5a87" hidden="false" page="56" publicationId="02e1-3f69-7ae7-f5c5">
      <description>Any foe in close combat with the Fiend counts any fumble rolls at double value. At the same time, any critical hits caused by the Fiend&apos;s enemy are ignored</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Split" id="b47b-ce1f-969f-c5db" hidden="false" page="59" publicationId="02e1-3f69-7ae7-f5c5">
      <description>When a Pink Horror is slain place it on its side rather than removing the model from play. At the end of the turn, remove the model and replace it with two Blue Horrors. 
May not divide into Blue Horrors if killed by Vortex Grenades, any type of webber, Distortion cannon, Wraith cannon, and the Daemonic Attack force card. A Blue horror replacing a burning Pink Horror are not set on fire themselves</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tongue Attack" id="2bd0-3e1d-9171-3829" hidden="false" page="56" publicationId="02e1-3f69-7ae7-f5c5">
      <description>Attack is added to the rider&apos;s attacks in the normal way for cavalry models. If this attack dice is the highest scoring of the model&apos;s attack dice then the enemy&apos;s own combat score is reduced by D3 points.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
